      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "Based on the wiki, here\u0027s how the Hub keeps the Anthropic API key out of its own process environment:\n\n**The key mechanism is credential scoping to child processes.** According to [[credential-scoping]], the Hub never actually holds the Anthropic API key in its own process environment at all. Instead:\n\n1. **A local secrets loader** reads the key from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file at startup\n2. **The key is injected only into child processes** \u2014 immediately before spawning the Ingest agent (or Query agent), the credential is injected directly into that child process\u0027s environment variables\n3. **The Hub\u0027s own process environment is never mutated** \u2014 it never receives the key itself\n\nThis design means a compromised or misbehaving Hub process cannot leak the credential simply by inspecting its own environment \u2014 the key exists only inside the short-lived child process that actually needs it to call the Anthropic API. Both the Ingest agent and Query agent receive the credential using the same scoping model: injected at spawn, never inherited from or written into the Hub.",
